\begin{align*}
\left(\int_{-1}^{1} |f|^p\,dx\right)^{\frac{1}{p}} &\leq C\left(\int_{-1}^{1} |f'|^p\,dx+|1-p|\left(\int_{-1}^{1} |f|^p\,dx+|f(0)|^p\right)\right)^{\frac{1}{p}}.
\end{align*}

We have also obtained a similar inequality for functions defined on the interval $[0,1]$, as well as for functions defined on the entire real line $\mathbb{R}$, and have shown that the constant $C$ in the inequality is sharp in all these cases.
